ok   we start as root
ok   /bin/mkdir is setuid root
ok   /bin/rmdir is setuid root
ok   /tmp is a directory
ok   guest ran /bin/mkdir to a normal exit
ok   the directory exists, so the effective uid became root
ok   it is owned by guest, so the real uid stayed guest's
ok   and carries guest's group
ok   its mode is 0777
ok   its link count is 2, so it has both . and ..
ok   and the parent gained a link
ok   mknod as guest is refused
ok   unlink of a directory as guest is refused
ok   and guest cannot climb back to root
ok   so nothing was created behind the refusal
ok   guest ran /bin/rmdir to a normal exit
ok   the directory is gone
ok   and the parent has its link count back
